{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/tbl-toffoli-lp-stability-table2-data","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Table","doco:Table"],"label":"tbl:toffoli-lp-stability-table2-data","kind":"table","title":"Table 2 from prop:toffoli-lp-stability","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-toffoli-lp-stability"],"tags":["extracted-table"],"text":"toffoli-lp-stability-table2-data.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"tbl:toffoli-lp-stability-table2-data\"></a>\n<strong>Table.</strong> <em>Table 2 from prop:toffoli-lp-stability</em></p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code> regime</th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">P_{7,7}(q)</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">P_{7,6}(q)</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\">Sign pattern</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0 &#x3C; q &#x3C; 1</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\">positive</td>\n<td align=\"center\">positive</td>\n<td align=\"center\">both positive</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q = 1</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1/2</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\">classical limit — the off-diagonals trivialise</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q > 1</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\">positive</td>\n<td align=\"center\"><strong>negative</strong></td>\n<td align=\"center\">mixed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q = q_0 \\approx 1.110</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\approx 0.6912</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\approx -0.1438</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\">mixed (substrate)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Convention <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">D</code> throughout. The sign pattern above is the inverse, on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q > 1</code>, of the one this table carried while it quoted the retired <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Phi</code>. Whether the mixed pattern is compatible with LP feasibility is <strong>open</strong> — see item 4 of the parent proposition; no physicality verdict is asserted per regime.</p>\n"}
